From 2fd36b48264ee7f15ed644207799ca93f4d1b1c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mita5358 <kafitcohr@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:33:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/20] perf(dsh): present a settled result card when its chunk
 loads
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A resume seed translated 93k events of the titan record in 1,838 ms, and
`presentResultView` was 730 ms of it: every settled result ran its card's
presenter over the result text, including the ~15.6k results that back
chunks the transcript only keeps as a digest row. Nothing renders those
cards until a chunk materializes, so the work is moved to that moment.

`translateReplay` takes `{ present: false }` for the seed; each chunk then
derives its payload from the result's own durable event through the same
`presentResultView`. The derivation is the translator's rule restated
(name and arguments from `tool/call`, skipped for `ask_user_question` and
subagent calls, errors left alone), so the rows are identical to an eager
translate — verified over all 93,121 translated entries of the titan log
(`/tmp/verify-defer.mjs`: 434 card payloads, no differences).

Measured on the mirror's titan session: `translate-done` 1,838 ms ->
1,083 ms of the boot trace, first paint 14,102 ms -> 13,718 ms.
